# How many people live in extreme poverty?
subtitle: "Guess the share of the world living on under three dollars a day, today and in 1990, and see how far it has fallen in one generation."

## How many people live in extreme poverty?
sources:
    - id: wb
      title: Poverty and Inequality Platform, June 2025 update (international poverty line $3.00 a day, 2021 prices)
      authors: World Bank, via Our World in Data
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/share-of-population-in-extreme-poverty
      finding: 'share of the world below $3 a day: 43.4 % in 1990, 10.1 % in 2024; world population 5.3 billion in 1990, about 8.2 billion in 2024'

    text y1990 "1990" cites ["wb"] x 250 y 690 font_size 40 hidden true
    text y2024 "2024" cites ["wb"] x 750 y 690 font_size 40 hidden true
    population then fit.h 440 fit.w 400 fit.x 60 fit.y 200 count 100 states.healthy 57 states.sick 43 order rows labels.healthy "above $3 a day" labels.sick "under $3 a day" hidden true
    population today fit.h 440 fit.w 400 fit.x 540 fit.y 200 count 100 states.healthy 90 states.sick 10 order rows labels.healthy "above $3 a day" labels.sick "under $3 a day" hidden true

What share of the world lives in extreme poverty? That means living on less than three dollars a day, adjusted for what money buys where you live.
    draw y2024

    ask "Out of every hundred people alive today, how many live like that? Mark them." on today_sick store t default "40" tolerance 0.05
        right: You said {t}: right, about {t.true}.
        wrong: You said {t}. It is about {t.true}, fewer than most people think.

Now go back a generation, to 1990.
    draw y1990

    ask "And in 1990, how many out of every hundred? Mark them." on then_sick store p default "50" tolerance 0.06
        right: {p}: close. It was {p.true}.
        wrong: You said {p}. It was {p.true}.

So from more than four in ten to about one in ten, in one generation, while the world grew by nearly three billion people.
    text growth "+2.8 bn people" x 500 y 690 font_size 28
